<title>USA: Quaker State settles pollution case - U.S.</title>
<headline>Quaker State settles pollution case - U.S.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quaker State Corp agreed to spend $3 million to settle charges it contaminated the environment at its petroleum-processing refinery in West Virginia, two federal agencies said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The U.S. Justice Department and the Environmental Protection Agency said the company agreed to pay a $1.75 million fine. The company will also spend $1.25 million to improve the pollution-control equipment at the facility near Newell.</p>
<p>The settlement resolved a 1993 lawsuit alleging that Quaker State had improperly stored and treated hazardous waste water and violated federal and state air pollution laws.</p>
<p>The state of West Virginia had joined in the lawsuit and the settlement.</p>
</text>
